{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Take heed regarding the plague of leprosy.</b> It was necessary to repeat this warning because it is a plague that strikes any person, even kings, as we find with Uzziah king of Judah, who was stricken — and it is a great disgrace. Therefore one must say that even if the king was stricken with leprosy, he must be distanced and done to according to all that the priests instruct. And therefore too it juxtaposed here: ״זכור את אשר עשה ה' אלהיך למרים״ — for she was the sister of the king and the sister of the high priest, and even so they distanced her and confined her like the rest of the lepers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:18.927384766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}